From 48015ada1c87970170f71bb0a3a731328ffeb007 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 20:14:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: close the two live false negatives in the
 protected-win gate, and mechanize the baseline boundary

CHECKER-R3 (independent, 2026-09-04) found two shapes that the fail-closed preflight PASSED. Both are fixed here, and both are fixed at the root rather than at the reported symptom.

D1, rename bypass. A 100%-similarity rename of a protected file passed the preflight. `git diff --name-only` reports only the DESTINATION path, so the protected path never entered `changed`; and a pure rename emits `similarity index 100% / rename from / rename to` with no content lines, so no protected anchor appeared as removed either. Both halves of the guard went blind on the one move that takes a win out from under its manifest entry while leaving the code intact. Fixed by passing `--no-renames` to BOTH git calls in `cmd_protected_win_check`, which turns the rename into delete+add and restores the path hit and the anchor lines together. Parsing `--name-status -M` would have fixed only the path half. CHECKED on the real range: `--no-renames` changes nothing on d7bd3bfca..upstream/master - 335 files either way, the same 6 collisions.

D2, measured-effect laundering. The classifier was prefix-ONLY, so a real measured win stated behind any of the thirty NO_EFFECT_PREFIXES was invisible to discover, validate, check and bump. It is the same class as the bare-dash bug the previous pass fixed, on the other thirty prefixes. Fixed by ORDER, not by another list entry: exact placeholders decide first, then a stated measured quantity makes the value REAL regardless of what prose precedes it, and the prefix vocabulary decides only when no quantity is present. Units that can only mean a rate or a duration count unconditionally; a bare `x` multiplier counts only when signed or decimal, because `2x16 GB` sizes a memory carve and does not report an effect.

THE D2 FIX PRODUCED A FINDING, not just a fix. Run against every Measured-effect trailer in d7bd3bfca..arifi/main (519 commits), the corrected classifier flips SIX commits from NO EFFECT to REAL. All six are pre-existing history and all six are ancestors of the ledger's own tip_when_recorded, so they were structurally invisible when protected-win-baseline.json was authored under the broken classifier. They are dispositioned here, each marked `_surfaced_by`, and the ledger prose is corrected from 24 rows to 30. This is a ledger completed, not a gate quieted: the strict set returns to 0 only because every one of the six now carries a written disposition, four of them REGISTRATION OWED.

D4, two re-dispositions under the President's capability law. bf0abf0be and 39a585bd5 were terminal as NO RUNTIME EFFECT on the ground that the format is OFF by default - while d0112ab49, f81c6dfdf and 159c3a21d, also inert on this seat, were REGISTRATION OWED under "zero on our seat is not zero". Same reasoning, opposite verdict, in one ledger. bf0abf0be's own trailer records a WORKING mechanism: a native ROCmFP4 artifact loaded in llama-server and completed, both ROCmFPX conformance suites pass, and Origin names it as ours. Default-OFF describes the shipped default, not the existence of the mechanism, and only the second is what this ledger protects. Both move to REGISTRATION OWED. Neither capability is discarded and no row is removed.

Counts, in both scopes, because one blended number would misread. Original 24 rows with D4 applied: 9 REGISTRATION OWED / 15 terminal. Plus the 6 surfaced by the D2 fix: 5 owed / 1 terminal. The ledger as a whole: 14 owed / 16 terminal / 30 rows.

BASELINE TAMPERING, closed by mechanism. The previous pass disclosed honestly that the baseline was closed to new shas BY CONVENTION - appending one line silenced the gate for a brand-new win forever. Disclosure is not a wall. `baseline_boundary_problems()` now refuses any row that is not an ancestor of the ledger's own `tip_when_recorded`, and refuses a missing or unresolvable boundary field so the hole cannot be reopened by deleting one line. Genuine history is untouched: all 30 rows are ancestors of bda5865cb, CHECKED per row.

Tests 22 to 34, stdlib only, all green. New: a protected rename is REFUSED and an unprotected rename still passes; all eight laundered shapes CHECKER-R3 reproduced classify REAL, driven through validate and the preflight and not only through the predicate; eighteen must-not-fire values still classify NO EFFECT; the bare-multiplier case both ways; discover and validate agree on the laundered set; and four boundary cases pinning both directions of the ancestry predicate, including that an empty baseline is not forced to invent one.

STILL OPEN, and no mechanism is claimed for it: manifest omission. An incoming change that deletes a mechanism no entry lists still passes check. That is inherent to an authored manifest and it is what discover exists to prevent upstream of.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Measured-effect: tooling and documentation only; no engine behaviour changed and no shipped default moved
WI: WI-1688
Lane: lane-209
Assisted-by: Opus 5 (guarded Max subscription wrapper)
